Subject: [PATCH] Always offer the shutter sound setting

MiuiCamera hides the camera sound entry, and forces the sound on regardless
of the stored preference, whenever it decides the handset is in a country
that requires it. The list is KR and JP, matched against the country code,
so a japanese handset never gets the setting at all.

The decision is one method. CameraPreferenceFragment skips adding
pref_camerasound_key when it returns true, v2.m3() ORs it over the stored
preference, and b4 - the thing that actually plays the sound - keeps it as
its "forced" flag. Returning false from it therefore does both halves at
once: the entry appears, and the switch it exposes is the one that decides.

Shutter sound in Japan is an industry practice rather than a legal
requirement, and this ROM leaves the choice where every other AOSP camera
leaves it - with whoever is holding the phone.

